# A preset: a typing of the canonical binary naturals, the filters
# `x ∥ binary_set true` that solo_own_loop_typing writes on a first-order
# loop's binders, enabled only together with the backend that represents
# those naturals (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Efficiency by design, with native structures").
#
# solo_own_loop_typing     the knowledge of one round, and of the library
#                          the round is compiled with
#
# The backend is not in this preset: the binary naturals' codecs
# (binary_prolog_backend), the natives of the binary operations
# (binary_operations_wren_backend), the candidacy and schemes of the binary
# naturals (binary_wren_shapes) and the typed versions that
# solo_own_loop_typing's typed branch is read through (wren_typed_block's
# wren_fixpoint_by_value and wren_typed_branch) are enabled through the
# preset corpora/compiler/wren_binary_preset. An entry that
# enables solo_own_loop_typing, in its knowledge or in a round, includes
# wren_binary_preset in its knowledge: typed without it, the loop's filters
# would type for no backend.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega corpora "compiler") "solo_own_loop_typing")
λ solo_own_loop_typing
. export solo_own_loop_typing
